---
import Layout from '../layouts/default.astro';
---
<Layout title="About me">
  <article class="about">
    <h1>About me</h1>
      <p>
        I consider myself a code craftsman with an insatiable curiosity for technology. My brain constantly toggles between problem-solving mode and hunting for elegant solutions. I've been known to enthusiastically explain proper software architecture to anyone willing to listen (and sometimes to those who aren't).
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm a Staff Software Engineer at CarStory (now part of Vroom), where I help build and improve systems that make car buying smarter. When I'm not there, I run a small software development studio with a few friends, creating custom solutions and bringing website ideas to life. My coding journey began back in 2007 with HTML and CSS, and I've been collecting languages and frameworks like trading cards ever since.
      </p>

      <p>
        I live in Serbia where I split my time between debugging code and debugging life. My family puts up with my tech obsessions because I occasionally emerge from behind my screens to be somewhat entertaining.
      </p>

      <strong>Tech Superpowers:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Software Architecture (I draw boxes and arrows with conviction)</li>
        <li>Technical Leadership (Guiding teams without making them roll their eyes... too much)</li>
        <li>Front-End Wizardry (Vue.js, Astro, Nuxt, etc.)</li>
        <li>Back-End Sorcery (Node.js, PHP, Go, etc.)</li>
        <li>Tool Mastery (git, docker, bash, tmux, neo(vim) etc.)</li>
        <li>CI/CD Magic (ansible, bash, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
.specialties {
  padding: 0 2em;

  & li {
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
}

a {
  text-decoration: underline;
  font-weight: 600;
}
</style>
